  "designIntent": {
    "firstRead": "A low scalloped maid headpiece and one continuous blue/white garment, not Lucario plus front plates.",
    "macroRules": [
      "No stacked horizontal cap slabs.",
      "No large rectangular bonnet plates beside the ears.",
      "No single rectangular apron board.",
      "No paired rectangular apron shields.",
      "No rigid folding-fan silhouette across the whole front.",
      "Use one narrow apron yoke plus two strongly angled overlapping lower cloth sheets instead of repeated vertical panels.",
      "Build the dress silhouette through overlapping side drapes that bridge front and rear cloth.",
      "The headpiece uses short staggered folds below the ear roots plus small side ties; it must not become a forehead bar or cover the face.",
      "Keep both ears and the face visually open.",
      "Carry white/periwinkle cloth through head, torso, sleeves, hips, front and rear.",
      "Spend geometry on contour changes, not repeated identical blocks."
    ],
    "referenceTechniqueCarryover": [
      "Two-stage parented drape and edge hierarchy from the inspected Ruins Style technique study.",
      "Whole-body costume continuity and anatomy-following shells from the inspected Space Style technique study.",
      "Connected head/torso garment hierarchy and animation-parented overlays from the inspected Covert Style technique study."
    ],
    "iterationNote": "Run 7 passed the technical visual floor at pixelDifferenceRatio 0.218694 and silhouetteDeltaRatio 0.049373, but manual front/profile QA rejected the two large white bonnet side plates. Run 8 removes those masses completely and rebuilds the head treatment as a low staggered five-fold front arc, a shallow rear bridge and two small asymmetric side ties. Garment geometry remains the run-7 wrap so this pass isolates head readability rather than moving every variable at once."
  },
